# Test: after a start refused for an external plugin's YANG module, the next
#       ze doctor reports doctor-plugin-schema-refused, with no daemon running
#
# Question: when `ze start` refuses the module an external plugin declared and
# exits, does `ze doctor`, run afterwards with no daemon, name the refusal
# under doctor-plugin-schema-refused, with the plugin, the module and the time?
# Why not a unit test: TestSchemaStopSurvivesTheRefusedStart proves the record
# is written and cleared, and TestSchemaStopRowsNameTheCodeTheCauseAndTheFix the
# row the check builds from it. Only the two runs prove that boot writes the
# record on the join's refusal, before any plugin server exists, and that the
# local doctor process, which registers no statestore, reads it from the
# store it opens. That a clean start deletes the record is the unit test's
# (Server.settleLastStop): it is the path doctor-plugin-fatal-stop already
# takes.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-14 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup: the code survives
#   the failed start (server.RecordRefusedSchemaStop, cmd/ze/hub/main.go; the
#   plugin-fatal-stop check, plugin/doctor/check_lifecycle_local.go).
# PREVENTS: a refusal that lives only on the terminal and in the log of a
#   process that is gone, so doctor says nothing of why ze is down.
#
# The form is the one of test/plugin/doctor-plugin-fatal-stop.ci, whose header
# gives the reason for each option: the disk store outlives the daemon, one
# budget for the whole file, and the doctor's SSH probe on this test's own
# port. The driver starts `ze start running.conf`, waits for the process to
# exit and refuses every result except exit 1, which is what a refused start
# returns (runYANGConfig, cmd/ze/hub/main.go).
option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT
tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bus {
	endpoint broken-module {
		external {
			run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang invalid";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/doctor-fatal-stop:exit=0
expect=stderr:contains=error: external plugin schema:
expect=stderr:contains=doctor-plugin-schema-refused
expect=stderr:contains=created live store:
reject=stderr:contains=could not record why ze is stopping
reject=stderr:contains=created memory store
reject=stderr:contains=Ze running.

# The daemon is gone, so the ask fails and the local checks answer. The
# plugin-fatal-stop check reads meta/plugin/last-stop from the store beside
# running.conf. The reject proves the entry did not fall to the fatal-stop
# row, which is what an unknown reason reads as.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze doctor --json config running.conf
expect=stdout:contains="code": "doctor-plugin-schema-refused"
expect=stdout:pattern=ze refused to start at [0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}Z because it refused a YANG module an external plugin declared
expect=stdout:contains=broken-module
expect=stdout:contains=acme-broken-conf
reject=stdout:contains="code": "doctor-plugin-fatal-stop"
